in Hawaii more evacuation orders have  been given to residents who live in the  path of lava pouring out of the Kilauea  volcano already thousands of people have  been forced to flee to safety dozens of  homes have been destroyed anyone who  stays could face arrest dangerous lava  flows have closed sections of the main  highway Kilauea has been erupting for  four weeks and that is hurting a big  business for the island tourism here's  Carter Evans with the latest river of  molten rock burning a new path to the  ocean people in nearby Kapoho have spent  the last two days packing up their homes  anticipating the lava would cut off the  last road out of their community in  Leilani estates Robert and Kristi Marin  want to stay as long as possible but  with a lava fountain four blocks away  from their home they're not spending  their nights here authorities now say  anyone who defies a new mandatory  evacuation order in Leilani estates  could be arrested the lava zone is  becoming increasingly dangerous  especially near the main fissure when  the lava comes it consumes everything in  its path but sometimes it burns these  trees down slowly you can see where it's  surrounded a trunk over there further to  the left that one is about to fall over  longtime residents say this could be the  new normal  what do you think the next month is  gonna look like unfortunately you're  probably looking at it and the dramatic  images broadcast around the world are  having another impact on tourism it was  kind of a shocker for us because this is  really a normal occurrence Ross Burgess  with the Big Island Visitors Bureau he  says the eruption impacts less than 1%  of the island but still hotel bookings  are down 50% even in Kona on the other  side of the island cruise ships are also  canceling port calls that's actually the  largest impact that we've had  specifically to the island is the  immediate lack of port calls both in  Hilo and in Kona and that really hurts  our mom-and-pop operations so do people  need to worry oh absolutely not  if you have plans to come to Hawaii  definitely keep those plans if you  hadn't had  right now it's actually the time to  start looking at it the Hawaii Volcanoes  National Park is the number one  attraction here but it's closed  indefinitely and scientists aren't  offering a prediction for how long this  eruption might last they are saying they  do expect more steam explosions at the  volcano's summit for CBS this morning  Saturday Carter Evans the Big Island of  Hawaii
 

